// The tab book that shows LilyPond's TWO-STAGE tab slur on paper, and the only one whose
// slurs can be COMPARED with LilyPond, because it removes the variable that stops the others:
// every note names its string (\4 \3 \2 \1), so the two engines cannot pick different strings.
// Their fret/string allocators do not agree, and a slur hangs off the DIGIT, so a book that
// leaves the choice open compares two fingerings rather than two slurs. Same device as
// test/tab-string-pinned, which does it for the beam.
//
// Bass tuning E1 A1 D2 G2, and a tab frets the SOUNDING pitch (written -12), so every note
// here is fret 5 on its own string: the fret is constant and only the STRING moves.
//
// ⚠️ BOTH DIRECTIONS, and that is the subject. LilyPond's slur direction reads the STRING,
// not the notated pitch (lily/slur.cc:60-68 calc_direction — UP as soon as one encompassed
// column's stem points DOWN). Bar 1 sits on the two HIGH strings (tab positions 1, 3, 3, 1;
// stems down) and must bow UP; bar 2 is its EXACT REFLECTION on the two LOW ones
// (−1, −3, −3, −1; stems up) and must bow DOWN. Until 2026-09-01 Lily# bowed every tab slur
// UP from an invented arch, so bar 2 is the half of this book that a snapshot of the old
// code could never show.
// ⚠️ REFLECTED, not merely "the other direction". Written as 4,3,3,4 the second bar is still
// a slur-down book, but its ENDPOINTS sit on the outer string where bar 1's sit on the inner
// — so the two numbers are unrelated and the pair asserts nothing. Reflected, LilyPond
// answers exact negatives, and a constant absorbed on one side cannot hide.
//
// What LilyPond does, in two stages (ly/engraver-init.ly:1248-1256 and :1275 →
// scm/lily/tablature.scm:144-157): ⑴ the ORDINARY slur scorer runs over bare fret digits —
// the TabStaff zeroes Stem.details "to minimize their influence on the
// slur::calc-control-points routine" — then ⑵ all four control points move
// staff-space × direction × 0.35 = 0.525 back toward the numbers.
//
// Measured against LilyPond 2.26.0 (audit/lp-geometry/probes/tab-slur.ly dumps
// control-points), in the tab staff's own spaces above its middle:
//   up    P0  1.043326  C1  2.074551      down  P0 −1.043326  C1 −2.074551
// exact negatives. The same two bars are ledger points slur.tab.*; the residuals there are
// the larger fret digits (ratified, docs/HANDOFF.md §3) and nothing else.
octave absolute
time 4/4
key c major

part bl { clef bass tuning bass }

section A {
  bl {
    g,4\2( c\1 c\1 g,\2) |
    d,4\3( a,,\4 a,,\4 d,\3) |
  }
}

form main { A }

score main {
  tab bl as numbers
}

// ⚠ `as numbers` ON PURPOSE, matching the twin's PLAIN `\new TabStaff`: the two stages are
// what the DEFAULT tab does, and `\tabFullNotation` reverts the stem overrides stage ⑴
// depends on. A tab-only score would otherwise default to `as full`.
